  "observations": [
    "One Files initial certificate required existing Caddy/ACME owner retries after authorization/finalization protocol errors; same pinned client succeeded without manual retry/restart. Provider-internal root cause unestablished.",
    "One Chat browser helper awaited an absent final-page Load more button. The confirmed rows were already present; corrected DOM-append wait passed the affected case without changing app assertions.",
    "A private Files fixture initially used active-detail GET for Trash and received the correct404; it was corrected to query the Trash list in a new namespace. Completed fixtures were retained until host destruction.",
    "One assigned Chat recovery IP was intercepted by the controller network (HTTP302 SafeBrowse on port443) while normal server-side loopback/public-IP TLS passed. Before any app restore, the exact installer wait was cancelled, absence of app/data/locks rechecked, that unused host destroyed, and a single separately recorded fresh-IP host used. No filter or TLS checks were disabled.",
    "Private cloud readiness initially read an asynchronous new Droplet network before active; corrected ordering reused the same recorded resource with no create replay."
  ],
